  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $4+8+16+\\,\u22ef?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=4$ and $r=2.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{4(1-{2}^{N})}{1-2} \\\\  & =-4(1-{2}^{N}) \\\\  & =4({2}^{N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
